# Context menu

Context Menu exposes actions at the pointer location. It supports right-click, `Shift+F10`, the Context Menu key, roving keyboard focus, viewport collision handling, outside click, and focus restoration.

Context menus are modal by default. A transparent backdrop blocks background clicks and hover previews without dimming the page. An outside primary click only dismisses the menu and returns focus to its trigger; it does not activate the control underneath. Tab stays in the menu, and Escape closes it. Use `modal={false}` on `AesirContextMenu`, or `modal="false"` on the HTML element, when background interaction is intentional.

